## 2. Remote Machine Portability

- [requirements.txt](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/requirements.txt):
  - Pinned to local versions: `numpy==2.5.2`, `scipy==1.18.1`, `pandas==3.0.6`, `matplotlib==3.11.2`, `h5py==3.16.0`, `pytest==9.1.1`, `torch==2.14.1`, `flyvis==1.2.0`, `datamate==1.0.0`.
  - Added PyTorch CUDA index documentation (`cu124` / `cu121`) for remote GPU VMs / clusters.
- [scripts/setup_remote.sh](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/scripts/setup_remote.sh):
  - Idempotent remote environment initialization.
  - Creates virtual environment via `uv venv` (falling back to `python3 -m venv`).
  - Downloads MPI Sintel complete and depth-training archives via `curl -C -` with `User-Agent: kagpt-fly-research`.
  - Extracts archives using Python's `zipfile` module (eliminating system `unzip` dependencies) and cleans up archives.
  - Resolves `flyvis.sintel_dir` dynamically and symlinks to `$DATA_DIR` (supports custom `DATA_DIR`).
  - Pre-generates null connectomes (`python nulls.py --seeds 0 1 2`) and runs `python -m pytest -q tests`.
- [scripts/grid.tsv](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/scripts/grid.tsv):
  - 24 pre-registered rows:
    - 15 rows: models `m1`–`m5` × seeds `0, 1, 2` at `data_fraction=1.0`.
    - 9 rows: models `m1, m2, m5` × seeds `0, 1, 2` at `data_fraction=0.25`.
    - Configured with placeholder variables `$N_ITERS` and `$LR`.
- [scripts/run_grid.sh](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/scripts/run_grid.sh):
  - Resumable: automatically skips runs with completed `runs/<name>/summary.json`.
  - Supports configurable concurrency per GPU (`JOBS_PER_GPU`, default 1) across single/multi-GPU setups.
  - Redirects logs to `runs/<name>/stdout.log`.
  - Supports optional per-run wall-clock timeout (`TIMEOUT`).
  - Validated dry-run mode (`DRY_RUN=1 scripts/run_grid.sh`).
- [scripts/slurm_array.sbatch](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/scripts/slurm_array.sbatch):
  - SLURM batch array template (`#SBATCH --array=1-24`) mapping tasks to `grid.tsv` rows.
- [README.md](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/README.md):
  - Two-paragraph problem statement and pre-registered hypotheses from [PLAN.md](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/PLAN.md).
  - Model M4 parameter matching and factory switch guide.
  - Local (CPU) and remote (GPU) quick-start guides.
  - Experiment grid execution and SLURM instructions.
  - Test evaluation protocol using `eval.py` (strict test-once policy).
  - End-to-end reproduction guide, data citations (Butler et al., ECCV 2012; Lappalainen et al., Nature 2024).
- [REPORT_AGY_2.md](file:///home/user/flyproj/course/REPORT_AGY_2.md):
